Id: sudo003w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_sudo
References: sudoers(5)
Controls: CIS 5.4; NIST AC-6; ISO 8.2; CE User access control

A Defaults line turns off authentication (!authenticate): sudo asks
the users it applies to for no password at all, as if every rule had
NOPASSWD. With a plain "Defaults !authenticate" that is everyone sudo
lets in.

To fix it, remove the line with visudo, or narrow it (Defaults:user
!authenticate) to an account that truly needs it.
